{"candidates":[{"content":"shared mechanism: The isolated artifact's discriminator (run-record perturbation-sensitivity) shares mechanism with the audit protocols of SRC_001–SRC_004 in that both operationalize a single counterexample-falsification logic — a falsifying intervention (injected false claim or mutated output) must flip the verdict. Refuted if the isolated artifact demands population-level negative controls (as SRC_003 argues) rather than a single perturbation, or if the same falsification logic can be satisfied by restatement without genuine world-dependent operation.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"de1003fa36f266e625214369e9da0d789b7d3fcb0ecbfcf440dd2e14978533a6"},{"role":"dependence","target":"51f65c8e129297a9fdfff455256229e554ae30643116b43bf92d644ea5ad44f9"},{"role":"dependence","target":"a6072bf14a21b22eae9f54369a3c550443268339ded34ec868bed0e4e3fc6939"},{"role":"dependence","target":"084384ac0b1efc38e645e553d16b07fe6df4d95f42ea6929dc608639132c0df6"},{"role":"dependence","target":"c1ebc340c49a526970b1587b99bb111e11178557812e9eec92c5458c32f5c135"}],"typicality":0.75},{"content":"contradicts: The isolated artifact's single-run perturbation test contradicts SRC_003's claim that neither separation nor any single-run procedural criterion is sufficient for genuine independent verification, because a single trajectory cannot statistically distinguish a genuine process from a biased one. The isolated artifact asserts diagnostic sufficiency where SRC_003 asserts n=1 insufficiency. Refuted if a single-run ablation can be shown to have sufficient power to distinguish a restater from a genuine verifier at conventional significance levels without requiring a population of trials.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"a6072bf14a21b22eae9f54369a3c550443268339ded34ec868bed0e4e3fc6939"}],"typicality":0.6},{"content":"reduces to: The isolated artifact's run-record discriminating operation reduces to a special case of SRC_004's unifier — it operationalizes one dimension (operational independence) by inspecting whether the run record contains a falsification operation whose output is world-dependent. The source-independence dimension is bracketed but not negated. Refuted if the artifact's operationalization is shown to require source independence as a precondition to avoid systematic gameability, making the reduction lossy and incomplete.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"084384ac0b1efc38e645e553d16b07fe6df4d95f42ea6929dc608639132c0df6"},{"role":"dependence","target":"51f65c8e129297a9fdfff455256229e554ae30643116b43bf92d644ea5ad44f9"}],"typicality":0.55},{"content":"abstracts: The isolated artifact's perturbation-sensitivity test abstracts the causal-decorrelation criterion of SRC_005 from population-level error decorrelation to a single-run mechanistic test. The verdict's responsiveness to a counterfactual perturbation (swap execution result, inject false claim) is an instance of causal decorrelation at n=1: the verifier's verdict is decorrelated from the producer's claim if and only if the perturbation flips it. Refuted if causal decorrelation at n=1 is shown to be neither necessary nor sufficient for the population-level decorrelation that constitutes independence as SRC_005 defines it.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"c1ebc340c49a526970b1587b99bb111e11178557812e9eec92c5458c32f5c135"},{"role":"dependence","target":"de1003fa36f266e625214369e9da0d789b7d3fcb0ecbfcf440dd2e14978533a6"}],"typicality":0.4},{"content":"compatible with: The isolated artifact's single-run ablation test is compatible with SRC_001's falsification-capacity criterion — both require that the record show an operation whose result could have contradicted the claim — but extends it from a static property of the record to a dynamic counterfactual test. The ablation operationalizes 'could have contradicted' by actually attempting the contradiction. Refuted if the falsification-capacity criterion can be fully satisfied by inspecting the record without perturbation, rendering the dynamic test redundant rather than complementary.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"de1003fa36f266e625214369e9da0d789b7d3fcb0ecbfcf440dd2e14978533a6"},{"role":"dependence","target":"084384ac0b1efc38e645e553d16b07fe6df4d95f42ea6929dc608639132c0df6"}],"typicality":0.3},{"content":"depends on: The isolated artifact depends on SRC_002's claim that genuine verification requires an operation whose output is not derivable from the claim text. The perturbation-sensitivity test presupposes this information-theoretic gap between the check and the claim: if the verdict is derivable from the claim text alone, no perturbation will flip it, correctly identifying restatement. Refuted if the information-theoretic criterion (non-derivability) is shown to be neither necessary nor sufficient for genuine verification, undermining the test's theoretical foundation.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"51f65c8e129297a9fdfff455256229e554ae30643116b43bf92d644ea5ad44f9"},{"role":"dependence","target":"c1ebc340c49a526970b1587b99bb111e11178557812e9eec92c5458c32f5c135"}],"typicality":0.2}],"simulation_proposals":[]}